<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugoslav July industry output down 0.2 pct mth/mth.</title>
<headline>Yugoslav July industry output down 0.2 pct mth/mth.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT (JULY)   (JUNE)     (JULY 96)</p>
<p> pct change mth/mth	   - 0.2     + 0.9	-  3.1</p>
<p> pct change yr/yr	     + 9.7     + 6.7	+ 15.7</p>
<p> index (base average 1996)  103.9     104.1	  99.4</p>
<p>CUMULATIVE DATA (JAN TO JULY)</p>
<p> pct change yr/yr	     + 8.1     + 8.0	 + 3.8</p>
<p>SEASONALLY ADJUSTED DATA</p>
<p> index (base average 1996)    116.3   103.9	  106.5</p>
<p>NOTE - July industry output was 42.5 percent lower than July 1991, before the breakup of the former Yugoslavia.</p>
<p>Cumulative January-July output was 52.7 percent below the same seven-month period in 1991.</p>
<p>Data largely exclude private sector, where manufacturing is not significant. Data cover Federal Republic of Yugoslavia, comprising Serbia and Montenegro.</p>
<p>- Beti Bilandzic, Belgrade newsroom +381 11 311 4305</p>
